# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLIENT ENVIRONMENT (safe to commit as .env.example)
#
# The frontend deliberately holds NO secrets. It never talks to the weather
# provider directly — it only calls this app's own backend, which keeps the
# provider (and any API key) server-side.
#
# In development, Vite proxies /api to the backend (see vite.config.ts), so you
# usually do NOT need to set anything here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OPTIONAL. Base URL of the backend API in production (e.g. when the frontend is
# hosted on Vercel and the backend on Render). Leave blank to use same-origin
# "/api" requests. Must be exposed with the VITE_ prefix to reach the browser —
# this is a PUBLIC URL, never a secret.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.onrender.com

# OPTIONAL. Override the dev-server proxy target (defaults to http://localhost:5000).
# VITE_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:5000
